WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.098
A class combines state and behavior.

00:00:02.248 --> 00:00:05.926
Encapsulation protects rules by limiting how state can change.

00:00:06.076 --> 00:00:11.704
An interface describes a capability, allowing implementations to vary without changing callers.

00:00:11.854 --> 00:00:17.126
Prefer composition when one object uses another capability; inheritance is useful only

00:00:17.126 --> 00:00:20.641
when the subtype genuinely satisfies the parent contract.

00:00:20.791 --> 00:00:27.289
Records provide concise data carriers and generated equality, accessors, and string representation.

00:00:27.439 --> 00:00:32.478
They are useful for request and response DTOs, but JPA entities have

00:00:32.478 --> 00:00:34.578
different lifecycle and proxy requirements.

00:00:34.728 --> 00:00:38.103
Exceptions should represent meaningful failure categories.

00:00:38.253 --> 00:00:42.585
Catch an exception only where you can recover, translate it into a

00:00:42.585 --> 00:00:46.195
useful boundary contract, or add context without losing the cause.

00:00:46.345 --> 00:00:51.793
JavaBasics.Discount is an interface whose implementation can calculate a discount without knowing

00:00:51.793 --> 00:00:52.701
about Spring.

00:00:52.851 --> 00:00:56.854
InventoryService has domain-specific Missing and Conflict failures.

00:00:57.004 --> 00:01:02.297
The HTTP layer translates these into 404 and 409, preserving the distinction

00:01:02.297 --> 00:01:05.384
between an absent product and insufficient stock.

00:01:05.534 --> 00:01:08.562
Implement fixed and percentage discount strategies.

00:01:08.712 --> 00:01:12.304
Add a maximum discount rule and tests that a discount cannot make

00:01:12.304 --> 00:01:13.202
the total negative.

00:01:13.352 --> 00:01:17.213
Explain why a request DTO should not be the same object as

00:01:17.213 --> 00:01:18.179
a persistence entity.

00:01:18.329 --> 00:01:21.716
Inject the selected strategy into a calculation service.

00:01:21.866 --> 00:01:27.783
DTOs expose only the intended public contract; entities represent database state and

00:01:27.783 --> 00:01:31.727
may include internal fields, relationships, and mutable lifecycle.

00:01:31.877 --> 00:01:36.322
Keeping them separate prevents accidental API changes when mappings change.

00:01:36.472 --> 00:01:37.143
Question.

00:01:37.293 --> 00:01:39.002
What is dependency inversion?

00:01:39.152 --> 00:01:39.729
Answer.

00:01:39.879 --> 00:01:44.914
High-level policy depends on an abstraction rather than a concrete infrastructure detail.

00:01:45.064 --> 00:01:45.735
Question.

00:01:45.885 --> 00:01:47.339
When should you use a record?

00:01:47.489 --> 00:01:48.065
Answer.

00:01:48.215 --> 00:01:53.028
For a value-like data carrier whose shallow immutability and generated equality fit

00:01:53.028 --> 00:01:54.231
the intended semantics.
